 "note": {
  "status": "draft",
  "text": "Utility software helps to maintain, protect and tidy the computer:\n• antivirus: finds and removes malware (viruses, worms, spyware); keep it updated;\n• firewall: blocks unwanted network connections;\n• backup: copies files so they can be restored after loss or damage;\n• disk clean-up: removes unneeded temporary files to free space;\n• compression (zip): makes files smaller to save space or send them faster;\n• disk defragmenter: rearranges files on a hard disk so they load faster (not needed on an SSD).\nA device driver is a small program that lets the operating system communicate with a hardware device (a printer, a scanner, a graphics card). Without the right driver, a new printer may not work.",
  "checks": []
 },
 "worked_example": {
  "status": "draft",
  "vars": {
   "d": "a new printer that the computer does not recognise"
  },
  "problem": "What should be installed to make {d} work, and why?",
  "steps": [
   "Install the printer's device driver (from the maker or the OS update).",
   "The driver translates the OS's instructions into commands the printer understands."
  ],
  "answer": "Its device driver, so the OS can communicate with the printer.",
  "checks": []
 },
